1
00:00:03,099 --> 00:00:05,599
(Leonard:)Hey, Amy, what brings you
to our neck of the woods?

2
00:00:05,768 --> 00:00:08,558
(Amy:)Your Neurology Department
Ioaned me a cuIture of prions...

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:12,110
(Amy:)...for my research
on bovine spongiform encephalopathy.

4
00:00:15,069 --> 00:00:18,069
(Sheldon:)She popped by
to borrow a cup of mad cow disease.

5
00:00:21,117 --> 00:00:25,037
(Amy:)It's hard to make degenerative brain
maladies hilarious, yet somehow you do.

6
00:00:27,123 --> 00:00:29,253
(Howard:)That's fun to have in a lunchroom.

7
00:00:29,459 --> 00:00:32,249
(Amy:)The real fun starts
when you pick the rat to feed it to...

8
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:36,300
(Amy:)...and maybe you choose the beady-eyed
mother who's been biting you all week.

9
00:00:38,092 --> 00:00:41,682
(Howard:)Please, we're eating. Can we get that
off the table and change the subject?

10
00:00:41,846 --> 00:00:44,476
(Sheldon:)Can we? Stand back...

11
00:00:44,641 --> 00:00:49,141
(Sheldon:)...while I turn this conversation
into a "conver-sensation."

12
00:00:49,771 --> 00:00:51,101
This time, it's your fauIt.

13
00:00:51,856 --> 00:00:54,146
(Sheldon:)I have 100 alphabetized topics...

14
00:00:54,317 --> 00:00:57,817
...from "Artichoke: Come on, people,
it's just a giant thistle"...

15
00:00:57,987 --> 00:01:04,027
...to "Zzz:
The onomatopoetry of sleep."

